  "comments": "A few main groups are known, which differ by thickness of all details. Most noticeably differences are visible on reverse, where in addition the type <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">D</span> has new spelling in Arabic.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">I</span> - top of lily far from rim.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span> - top of lily far from rim. Circle under the coat of arms.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Note</span>. Different thickness of details.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span> - top of lily almost touches rim. Circle under the coat of arms.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61be653220835.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61be653220835.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"199\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - all details thick and far from rim, no hamza &#039;ء&#039; under alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039;.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - all details thick and close to rim.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span> - all details thin.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">D</span> - all details very thin, with hamza &#039;ء&#039; under alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039;.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61be65605c869.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61be65605c869.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"210\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\nCopper-nickel, medal alignment ↑↑<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">I</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>: 5745-5753.<br /><br />\r\nNickel plated steel, medal alignment ↑↑<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 5754-5763.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span>: 5765-5767.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">D</span>: 5769-5777.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 5757.<br /><br />\r\nNickel plated steel, coin alignment ↑↓<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 5754.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span>: 5766.",
